From 085d2065ffbd7ac834dd32677e3889f8163b71a3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 10:30:17 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] metal: replace the garbled library loader with upstream's
 per-kind loader plus an ArifiLabs library kind

ggml-metal-device.m at 3f3011efa could not compile in either library mode.
Mechanism, CHECKED: upstream split the Metal source into per-kind libraries
in b615f5b4b (2026-08-25, before the b10680 base) and rewrote the loader
around GGML_METAL_LIBS / objs[] / fn_to_lib. The fork's device.m hunks were
authored on the pre-split loader (patch 0006-laguna, 37af31769) and every
base move since kept the fork side of the conflicting hunks, so the file
became the old single-library init spliced into the new loader: it used
GGML_METAL_LIB_COUNT, k_lib_names, ggml_metal_library_compile_all and
lib->fn_to_lib with none of their definitions, defined
ggml_metal_device_init(int) against a two-argument declaration in the
header, and dropped ggml_metal_device_id_token, the virtual-device naming,
the gpu_family probe and the autoreleasepool leak fixes.

The union takes upstream b10819's device.m whole and re-applies the fork's
mechanisms onto it:
- TURBO_USE_4MAG / TURBO_SPARSE_V / TURBO_PROFILE_MODE preprocessor macros in
  the shared compile options
- supports_op: asymmetric turbo/q8_0 K/V pairs and the turbo types in
  FLASH_ATTN_EXT, GGML_OP_TURBO_WHT, turbo types in CPY/SET_ROWS, TQ3_1S and
  TQ4_1S as CPY sources, the im2col KH*KW > 1024 decline (gemma4uv)
- a 21st library kind ARIFI whose source is the monolithic ggml-metal.metal.
  The fork's 593 monolith-only kernel names (TQ/TurboQuant/ROCmFPX/Escha and
  the turbo FA instantiations) live nowhere else; the monolith also carries
  older copies of 522 upstream kernel names, so the routing index is now
  first-wins and ARIFI is last: the split library keeps every name it
  defines (including the 318 tuned _q#_ne# vec kernels the monolith lacks),
  ARIFI serves only the names the split does not have.

CMakeLists.txt follows the same shape: ggml-metal-tuning.cpp is back in the
source list beside ggml-metal-moe-cache.mm (the fork's list had dropped it);
embed=ON emits ggml_metallib_arifi_{start,end}; embed=OFF compiles the
monolith into its own ggml-arifi.metallib, never into default.metallib
(shared kernel names would collide at metallib link), and the loader picks
it up next to default.metallib exactly like ggml-tensor.metallib.

NOT compiled: no Metal toolchain on this estate. Balance checked (braces,
parens, brackets 0), every identifier resolves in the file or ggml.h. The
metal-macos jobs now also require ggml-metal-moe-cache.mm.o and the arifi
library artifact for their mode, so a build that silently drops the
ArifiLabs kernel set fails there.

Origin: ArifiLabs lane-210 R17C (Fable 5.1 MEDIUM, kernel-maker), union of upstream b10819 6a1a922d2 ggml-metal-device.m/CMakeLists.txt with the fork hunks of 37af31769 and 95c1b6e69
Measured-effect: UNMEASURED - off-rig backend, union-by-mechanism-read; compile verification PENDING the first metal-macos run
WI: WI-1702, WI-1703
Lane: lane-210
